Irradiation experiments. For solid-state Raman spectroscopy, samples of motoMOF crystals were kept at room temperature, in a $1\mathrm{mm}$ capped quartz cuvette filled with DMF or between two quartz slides sealed with polytetrafluoroethylene paste to avoid drying. Raman spectra were acquired using a RamanStation400F (PerkinElmer) employing multimode fibres for both excitation and collection. The sample was placed on the Olympus BX51 microscope stage and a chosen single crystal of moto-MOF was aligned with the laser beam ( $785\mathrm{nm}$ , 50 mW) at $\times50$ lens magnification. Irradiations were carried with a $395\mathrm{nm}$ light-emitting diode (Thorlab M395F1) connected to a $0.6\mathrm{mm}$ optical fibre, which guided the light to the position of the laser beam.
